# proto-file: contracts/proto/vectra/config.proto
# proto-message: vectra.config.v1.IndexParams
#
# Index construction and query defaults for every shard.
#
# Capacity model (128-d corpus, 10M vectors over the cluster):
#   PQ codes        16 B/vector  -> 160 MB   (32x smaller than FP32 [22])
#   FP32 re-rank    512 B/vector -> 5.12 GB  (exact distances for the final
#                                             re-rank; see
#                                             docs/research/hnsw-parameter-study.md)
#   HNSW layer 0    4 + 4*m0 B   -> 1.32 GB  (m0 = 32 links as 32-bit offsets)
# Everything is RAM-resident and mlock'd.

dimension: 128
# HNSW [21]: M links per insertion, layer-0 cap 2*M (the paper's choice).
m: 16
m0: 32
ef_construction: 200
# 16-byte PQ codes need a re-rank beam of ~128-256 to hold recall@10 >= 0.95
# on high-intrinsic-dimension data; tune with benchmark/recall/.
ef_search: 128
rerank_depth: 128
# Per-shard reservation, including headroom for live ingest.
max_elements: 4000000
# 16 sub-quantizers x 8 bits = 16 bytes per vector.
pq_subspaces: 16
pq_training_samples: 65536
pq_kmeans_iterations: 25
# Radius populations up to this size are scanned exactly instead of
# traversing the graph with a selective filter.
exhaustive_scan_threshold: 2048
build_threads: 8
seed: 100
